  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.0 — first release.\n\nADDED:\n- GmailClient (IGmailClient): GetProfileAsync, ListMessagesAsync, GetMessageAsync, GetMessageRawAsync (MimeKit MimeMessage), ListHistoryAsync, ModifyLabelsAsync, BatchModifyLabelsAsync, TrashAsync, UntrashAsync, ReportSpamAsync, ListLabelsAsync, CreateLabelAsync, UpdateLabelAsync, DeleteLabelAsync, GetAttachmentAsync, DownloadAttachmentAsync, SendAsync (multipart upload of a MimeMessage through messages.send — the gmail.modify scope is enough, no SMTP).\n- GoogleOAuthClient (IGoogleOAuthClient): BuildAuthorizationUrl, ExchangeCodeAsync, RefreshAsync, RevokeAsync; GoogleOAuthOptions.FromConfiguration; GoogleIdTokenPayload.Parse (no signature verification, for tokens received directly from Google).\n- GmailApiException for every non-2xx response with StatusCode, Reason, ErrorMessage, ResponseBody and the IsUnauthorized / IsHistoryExpired / IsRateLimited / IsNotFound flags.\n- Exponential backoff retry (default 3 retries from 1s, honours Retry-After) for 429, 5xx and the 403 rate-limit reasons Gmail uses, configurable through GmailClientOptions.\n- Async only, ConfigureAwait(false) throughout, OperationCanceledException never wrapped; token storage is the caller's responsibility (an access-token provider delegate).\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/ozakboy/ozakboy.Gmail/blob/main/docs/en/changelog.md",
